[size=5][b]Map Markers[/b][/size]
[i]NPCs and points of interest on the world map, drawn as hand-inked parchment tags.[/i]

Open the map and see where everyone is right now. Every named NPC gets a small parchment tag with their portrait, cropped to a head-and-shoulders bust, and the tag's tip points at their exact position. Markers follow NPCs live while the map is open. Ore veins, fishing spots, caves and other useful places can be shown too, each category with its own pixel-art icon.

[size=4][b]FEATURES[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Live NPC positions[/b]: markers update while the map is open, using the same projection as the game's own player icon, so they line up with the map art.
[*][b]Portrait busts[/b]: the game's NPC portraits are cropped to a head-and-shoulders bust automatically; the blue outline is re-inked to match the map.
[*][b]Retro look[/b]: semi-transparent parchment tags with an ink border, drop shadow and a pointer tip, rendered as crisp pixel art at a configurable pixel size. No image files are shipped; all art is generated at runtime.
[*][b]Names on hover[/b]: in the game's language, or always shown, or hidden. Works with a gamepad too: move the map cursor onto a marker and it snaps on and shows the name.
[*][b]Town vendors[/b]: the shops you build in town get a marker with the vendor's portrait; hover to see the vendor type (Apothecary, Baker, ...).
[*][b]No pile-ups[/b]: NPCs standing close together, or inside the same building, are spread side by side, with an ink line to where each one really is.
[*][b]Fog of war respected[/b]: unexplored areas still cover markers.
[*][b]Points of interest[/b], each switchable in the Mods menu:
[list]
[*]Ores & quarries: iron ore, copper vein, marble and stone quarries, sand and clay pits
[*]Fishing spots: the label shows how many fish are left; the marker fades when the spot is empty
[*]Caves & descents: cave passages, the mine, sewer entrances, descent ladders, blocked caves
[*]Portals
[*]Optional, off by default: teleport pillars (the vanilla map already shows them), common stones, doors & basements
[/list]
[*][b]Fully configurable[/b] through the GK2 Mod Framework Mods menu: every category has on/off, match rules, color, icon, scale and label mode.
[*][b]Can be toggled at runtime[/b] from the Mods menu; disabling removes every patch and marker.
[/list]

[size=4][b]REQUIREMENTS[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Graveyard Keeper 2 (Steam, Windows x64)
[*][url=https://github.com/BepInEx/BepInEx/releases/tag/v5.4.23.5]BepInEx 5.4.23.5 x64[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/graveyardkeeper2/mods/42]GK2 Mod Framework[/url] 0.1.x
[/list]

[size=4][b]INSTALLATION[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install BepInEx 5.4.23.5 x64 and GK2 Mod Framework.
[*]Extract this archive into the Graveyard Keeper 2 folder so the DLL ends up at [font=Courier New]BepInEx/plugins/GK2.MapMarkers.dll[/font].
[*]Start the game and open the map. Settings: main menu → [b]Mods[/b] → [b]Map Markers[/b] → Settings.
[/list]
Loading can be verified in [font=Courier New]BepInEx/LogOutput.log[/font]: look for [font=Courier New]MAP_MARKERS_ENABLED[/font].

[size=4][b]UPDATING / UNINSTALLING[/b][/size]
Close the game and replace, or delete, [font=Courier New]BepInEx/plugins/GK2.MapMarkers.dll[/font]. The mod does not touch save files. Settings live in [font=Courier New]BepInEx/config/a632079.gk2.mapmarkers.cfg[/font].
When you update, saved category rules that still equal an older default are upgraded automatically. Rules you edited yourself are kept.

[size=4][b]SETTINGS[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]General[/b]: refresh interval, pixel size (screen pixels per art pixel; raise it for bigger markers), parchment opacity, spread overlapping markers
[*][b]NPC[/b]: on/off, named NPCs only or all NPCs, name labels, scale, portraits, head-only portraits, excluded NPC ids
[*][b]Town vendors[/b]: on/off, labels, scale, head-only portraits
[*][b]Each category[/b]: on/off, match rules, color, icon (pickaxe, fish, pillar, cave, ladder, coin, cross, star, gem), scale, labels
[*][b]Advanced[/b]: Ctrl+F9 writes every world-object id of the loaded save to [font=Courier New]BepInEx/MapMarkers_wgo_dump.txt[/font], so you can write your own rules
[/list]
Rule syntax: [font=Courier New]id:x[/font], [font=Courier New]prefix:x[/font], [font=Courier New]contains:x[/font], [font=Courier New]group:x[/font], [font=Courier New]type:InteractionType[/font], and [font=Courier New]!rule[/font] to exclude. Separate rules with commas.

[size=4][b]COMPATIBILITY[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Built for Steam build 25467846. Re-checked on build 25533739: none of the game code this mod uses changed.
[*]The mod does not require a known game build, so it keeps running after game updates. If a future update renames what it relies on, markers simply don't appear and an error is logged; the game does not crash.
[*]Not tested together with other map mods such as [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/graveyardkeeper2/mods/127]Interactive map[/url] or [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/graveyardkeeper2/mods/140]Map Click Teleport[/url]. With name labels set to Hover, a marker catches the mouse over its own small area, so a double-click exactly on a marker may not reach the map underneath. Set Labels to Always or Never to let clicks through.
[/list]

[size=4][b]KNOWN LIMITATIONS[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Early release: the NPC markers have been seen working in game, but not every point-of-interest rule has been checked in every area yet. Reports with a screenshot and the Ctrl+F9 dump are very welcome.
[*]NPCs in interiors that the map has no anchor for are not shown.
[*]Point-of-interest ids come from the game's data. If an update renames objects, adjust the rules in the Mods menu or wait for an update.
[/list]

[size=4][b]FOR MOD AUTHORS[/b][/size]
Other mods can add their own marker categories: implement [font=Courier New]IMapMarkerProvider[/font] and call [font=Courier New]MapMarkersApi.RegisterProvider(...)[/font], with a BepInDependency on [font=Courier New]a632079.gk2.mapmarkers[/font]. See the README on GitHub.

[size=4][b]SOURCE[/b][/size]
[url=https://github.com/greenhat616/GraveyardKeeper2NpcMapIndicator]GitHub: greenhat616/GraveyardKeeper2NpcMapIndicator[/url]

